@title Crash Bandicoot 2 - N-Tranced (USA)
@file Crash Bandicoot 2 - N-Tranced (U).gba
@game AC8E
@chip EEPROM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# New Game, skip the story, play the whole Island Intro tutorial level
# (Aku Aku hints, TNT, double jumps, bounce crate, R-slide under steel,
# crystal over a gap, double jump over a Nitro) into the exit portal;
# the game offers "Continue and save" > slot 1, then the map.
# [load]: title > Load Game shows 1% / 1 crystal, slot 1, resumed on the map.
# Findings: save files differ in size: dingbat-bios 512 bytes, mgba and nba
# 8192 bytes (same 16 data bytes in the first 512). Booted with its own file,
# nba shows 0% and every slot EMPTY and stays on the load screen, so nba's
# [load] checkpoints differ (dingbat-bios and mgba resume on the map).
# In play nba's Crash is often one animation frame off the others (e.g.
# f2738, f5211), positions agree.

